# Source-Grounded Feasibility Research

Status: DONE
Milestone: M0 Desk research only
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Establish documented mechanisms, limits, alternatives, and the experiments needed before implementation.

## Tasks

- [x] Verify Windows display-affinity values, HWND ownership, DWM, API floor, and non-security guarantee.
- [x] Separate taskbar/Alt-Tab behavior, native enumeration, capture-picker presence, and pixels.
- [x] Investigate WPF/native/WinUI/Electron/Tauri and their editor/runtime/distribution tradeoffs.
- [x] Verify current .NET support and packaging/signing considerations without inventing measurements.
- [x] Examine macOS/ScreenCaptureKit and bounded Linux contracts; avoid false universal parity claims.
- [x] Record getter/layered-window and composition/first-frame questions as empirical work.
- [x] Define required product/backend capture scenarios, controls, evidence, and failure boundaries.
- [x] Preserve source register, retrieval limits, proposed architecture and proof-first delivery workflow.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Major API/framework claims trace to retrieved primary sources in docs\FEASIBILITY.md.
- [x] Proposed stack/defaults are distinct from approved Windows 11 scope.
- [x] No research completion is presented as app implementation or tested product compatibility.
- [x] Unresolved runtime questions are assigned to workstreams 03, 06, and 13.

## Completion evidence

- docs\FEASIBILITY.md: 26 source-register groups, findings, limits, and experiment register.
- docs\ARCHITECTURE.md: proposed lifecycle/state/components and failure policies.
- docs\QUALIFICATION.md: unexecuted product matrix, controls, C01-C14, result schema.
- docs\DEVELOPMENT-WORKFLOW.md: G0-G5 delivery gates.
- No prototype, code benchmark, product capture test, or release qualification was run.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 (Asia/Kolkata) - Completed source synthesis from the October 7 UTC research session.
